# Release protocol

When the user says "Implement and PR this.", "Prepare this for release.", or "Deploy the approved release.", follow docs/engineering/RELEASE_PROTOCOL.md. Do not restate the product boundary.

Implement and PR never deploys. Prepare stops at READY FOR DEPLOYMENT. Deploy runs only when that same message names the artifact and the production target. Otherwise stop BLOCKED BEFORE CUTOVER.

Passing checks do not mean the pull request is merged. Do not weaken production protection.

A hosted shop release, including a communications-only change, runs Landlord `host/shop-release/shop-release.sh` through the `cursor-release` key. Never write a cutover script, start the shop container by hand, or use the shared root key. Diagnostics use the `cursor-comms` key.

End every feature response with one release state from that protocol. Only DEPLOYED AND HEALTHY means `lugsnplugs.arksms.com` is running it. `lnp.arksms.com` is an older deployment and is not that target.
